# Slice 332: g is the Structure merge copies from the Structure the declaration of f created in this traversal,
# not a function -- a function is the Structure the receiver fn creates (kernel §3.4: the result role marks it, not
# a Structure with similar parts; the author 2026-11-09: `fn: g merge(f)`, slice 333).
# The statement `g(1; 2)` has two operands and no operation: the interpreter answers 2.
fn: f (int: a; int: b) int (int: calls 0; int: last 0)
    calls: calls + 1
    last: a * 10 + b
    return: last
end: f
g: merge(f)
g(1; 2)
fn: pair (int: x) int
    g(3; 4)
    return: x + 1
end: pair
int: r pair(5)
g(b := 7; a := 6)
int: f_calls f\var\calls
int: f_last f\var\last
int: g_calls g\var\calls
int: g_last g\var\last
